<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav September industry output rises 6.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav September industry output rises 6.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  SEPT	AUG	  SEPT 95</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	   + 6.9     + 2.1	   N.A</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     +11.3     + 9.7	   N.A</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)  109.4     102.3	   N.A</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO SEPT)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     + 5.6     + 4.9	   N.A</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)  110.5     109.5	   N.A</p>
<p>NOTE - September 1996 output is down 42.2 percent against the same month in 1991.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-September 1996 output is down by 46.8 percent against the same period in 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. Data cover rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Beti Bilandzic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
